  "note": "Triennial election of Omagh Urban District Council, January 1929. Only the South Ward was contested: North Ward returned seven Unionists unopposed and West Ward seven Nationalists unopposed, while eight candidates stood for the seven South Ward seats (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1929, p. 12). The South Ward poll result has not been found, so the South Ward is not recorded. Labels are the paper's group labels. Returned unopposed."
